ian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:01:58-08:00","id":1177345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1176688-stupid-inanimae-questions?p=1177146#post1177146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But winds don't stay.. similar with fires. Sirocco do show up.. and then end. a Hurricane spreads itself through out over a couple of days.. clouds change etc</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're thinking a bit to big, I think. Imagine that one gust that always seems to move a field of grass, always blows through a corridor because the windows wont close or moves that dreamcatcher you own. Sure, it's not always blowing, but it's always &quot;there&quot;. It's not the physical movement of air, it's the concept of that gust, of that familiar draft that you anchor to (at least that's how I see it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T15:05:28-08:00","id":1177427,"title":"","content":"A Krofted Parsome anchor might include perfume","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat